# Base rules

## Doc map

- **Setup & commands** → [README.md](../../README.md)
- **System design & deployment** → [ARCHITECTURE.md](../../ARCHITECTURE.md)
- **Stack, paths & conventions** → [PROJECT.md](../../PROJECT.md)

## Scope

- Keep changes narrowly scoped to the request.
- Prefer clear names, small focused files, and arrow functions for non-trivial helpers and handlers.
- Keep files around 120 lines when practical; split by responsibility when they grow.

## TypeScript

- No `enum`.
- No `any` unless a short inline comment explains why.
- Prefer `unknown` for external data that still needs narrowing.

## Working style

- Read `PROJECT.md` first.
- Prefer targeted file reads and searches over broad repository sweeps.
- Add comments only when the intent is not obvious from the code itself.

## Repo hygiene

- Run `npm run fix` before pushing.
